{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh also called.</b> To include Pharaoh's wife, for she was the first to begin calling for the wise men and the sorcerers." "<b>They also.</b> He did not call at first except for infants, and afterward <b>for the wise men and the sorcerers</b> — therefore it is written ״ויעשו גם הם״ — 'they also did.' Rabbi Shimon ben Pazi said: what did they see to compare the daughter of the snake to the kingdom? For it is said (Jeremiah 46:22): ״קולה כנחש ילך״ — 'her sound goes like a snake.' Just as the snake slithers and goes, so the kingdom of Egypt bends its ways; just as the snake whispers and kills, so the kingdom of Egypt whispers and kills. [Moses] suspended the staff opposite Pharaoh and said to him: From this you are stricken." "<b>With their flames.</b> Acts of sorcery, and they are performed by means of angels of destruction. The word is derived from the language of (Psalms 104:4) ״אש לוהט,״ and (ibid. [Psalms] 106) ״להבה תלהט רשעים.״ The meaning is that they act by means of flaming angels of fire that burn within a man without his knowledge, and it kindles in him and he pays it no mind. And perhaps they are so called — the angels that dwell in the air within the spheres of the elements, which they call demons (שדים): בלטיהם — the deeds of demons. And they are called by this name because they come to a man secretly (בלט), because they possess bodies of air that are not perceived; and this is what is meant by ״for the wise men and for the sorcerers,״ for the masters of incantations and the gatherers of demons were their heads and elders, and ״the magicians (חרטומים) of Egypt״ includes both of them. And the word חרטומים is a compound word — חר טמי, that is, 'those examined (מוחררין) in bones,' for most of their craft is with bones of the dead or bones of living creatures. Thus wrote the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:51.174733428Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}